`xtask golden`'s usage errors, which stop before it reads the repository or
installs the oracle (exit status 2). `tests/golden/README.md` describes the
commands; the library's unit tests cover their parts.

```console
$ xtask golden help
usage: cargo xtask golden <command> [options]

commands:
  record [--check-determinism] [--filter GLOB] [--jobs N]
             run every case through the oracle and write tests/golden/cases/
             and COVERAGE.md. --check-determinism runs every case twice and
             fails, writing nothing, unless both runs agree byte for byte
  check [--engine python|rust|compare] [--filter GLOB] [--jobs N]
             run every case through the engine and compare with the
             recordings; also checks COVERAGE.md and that no recording is
             missing or orphaned
  diff [--engine ...] [--filter GLOB] [--jobs N]
             check, printing every difference in full
  lock       rewrite tests/golden/oracle-requirements.txt from ORACLE (uv pip compile)
  coverage   rewrite COVERAGE.md from cases.toml and the recordings

--filter GLOB  only the cases whose id (<command>/<mode>/<fixture>/<variant>) matches
--engine       python (the oracle, the default); compare: this repository's CLI with
               OPENTIDE_ENGINE=rust against the recordings, through the comparator
               and tests/golden/APPROVED_DIFFS.toml, for every case whose command
               has a Rust implementation (UC-0.7); rust comes with UC-3
               and cannot start until then (exit status 2)
--report FILE  with --engine compare: write the JSON report (opentide-compare's RunReport)

exit status: 0 passed, 1 a difference or a failed case, 2 usage error or the run could not start

$ xtask golden
? 2
xtask golden: missing command

usage: cargo xtask golden <command> [options]
...

$ xtask golden frobnicate
? 2
xtask golden: unknown command `frobnicate`

usage: cargo xtask golden <command> [options]
...

$ xtask golden record --engine rust
? 2
xtask golden: only the oracle records: `record` takes no --engine

$ xtask golden check --check-determinism
? 2
xtask golden: unknown option `--check-determinism` for this command

usage: cargo xtask golden <command> [options]
...

$ xtask golden check --jobs many
? 2
xtask golden: --jobs needs a number: invalid digit found in string

```
